### 2.11 Symbol Table Implementation using TAB Module (Slide 23)

**Code:**
```c
// make a new S_Table
S_table S_empty(void) {
    return TAB_empty();
}

// insert a binding
void S_enter(S_table t, S_symbol sym, void *value) {
    TAB_enter(t, sym, value);
}

// look up a symbol
void *S_look(S_table t, S_symbol sym) {
    return TAB_look(t, sym);
}
```

**Explanation:**
The Tiger compiler uses a **generic hash table module (TAB)** as the underlying implementation for S_table. The S_table interface is built on top of TAB, providing a clean abstraction. TAB is a generic hash table that uses symbols as keys (which enables fast hash and equality comparisons).

